cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released model weights, please cite the accompanying paper once its citation is available."
title: "ColFOV: semantic-guided four-class endoscopic frame segmentation with derived FOV and session PiP geometry"
abstract: >-
  ColFOV segments endoscopic frames into four classes (background UI, valid FOV tissue,
  black corner, popup overlay) and derives three geometry products from those masks: an
  inner-FOV box, a full-FOV box, and a conditional, causal session-level
  picture-in-picture box. The network outputs only the segmentation mask; all bounding
  boxes are derived geometry and abstain fail-closed when their evidence conditions are
  not met.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bgmseo/ColFOV"
authors:
  - family-names: "Seo"
    given-names: "Bo Geum"
    email: "bgm.seo@snu.ac.kr"
    affiliation: "Seoul National University"
keywords:
  - colonoscopy
  - endoscopy
  - semantic segmentation
  - field of view
  - picture-in-picture
